
  <sn><md>### Using `--dry-run` with rclone

The `--dry-run` option lets you **preview an rclone operation without making any actual changes**.

```text
NORMAL COMMAND
      │
      ▼
rclone performs the operation
      │
      ├── ✔️ Files copied
      ├── ✔️ Files moved
      └── ✔️ Files deleted


WITH --dry-run
      │
      ▼
rclone shows what would happen
      │
      ├── 🔍 Files that would be copied
      ├── 🔍 Files that would be moved
      └── 🔍 Files that would be deleted
           
      ❌ No actual changes
```

**Basic Syntax**

```bash
rclone COMMAND SOURCE DESTINATION --dry-run
```
