<sn><md>### Testing `sync` Safely

Suppose:

```text
SOURCE                       DESTINATION

📄 A.txt                     📄 A.txt
📄 B.txt                     📄 B.txt
                             📄 Old.txt
```

Run:

```bash
rclone sync SOURCE DESTINATION --dry-run
```

Rclone analyzes both locations:

```text
SOURCE                       DESTINATION

📄 A.txt                     📄 A.txt ✔️ Keep
📄 B.txt                     📄 B.txt ✔️ Keep
                             📄 Old.txt ❌ Would delete
```

But because you used `--dry-run`:

```text
DESTINATION AFTER DRY RUN

📄 A.txt
📄 B.txt
📄 Old.txt ✔️ Still exists
```

No files are actually deleted.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Examples

**Local to Cloud**

```bash
rclone sync ~/Documents mega:Backup --dry-run
```

Preview what would happen when synchronizing your local `Documents` folder with MEGA.

```text
💻 Local Documents ────────► ☁️ MEGA Backup
        Analyze only
              🔍
        ❌ No changes
```


**Cloud to Local**

```bash
rclone sync mega:Backup ~/Documents --dry-run
```

Preview the synchronization from MEGA to your local computer.

### **Cloud to Cloud**

```bash
rclone sync gdrive:Documents mega:Backup --dry-run
```

Preview synchronization between Google Drive and MEGA.
</md></sn><sn><md>### `--dry-run` with Other Commands

| Command  | Example                                    | Actual Changes? |
| -------- | ------------------------------------------ | --------------- |
| `copy`   | `rclone copy SOURCE DESTINATION --dry-run` | ❌               |
| `move`   | `rclone move SOURCE DESTINATION --dry-run` | ❌               |
| `sync`   | `rclone sync SOURCE DESTINATION --dry-run` | ❌               |
| `delete` | `rclone delete REMOTE:PATH --dry-run`      | ❌               |
</md></sn><sn><md>### Recommended Workflow

```text
Step 1
   │
   ▼
Run the command with --dry-run
   │
   ▼
Review the planned changes
   │
   ├── ❌ Something wrong → Stop and fix the command
   │
   └── ✔️ Everything correct
           │
           ▼
Step 2
   │
   ▼
Run the same command without --dry-run
           │
           ▼
      ✔️ Actual operation
```

&gt; ⚠️ Always use `--dry-run` before running an important `rclone sync` command, because `sync` may delete files from the destination.
</md></sn>